{
  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_031 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.678 acc. The image-only ResNet50 baseline was very weak (0.208 acc), yet it still contributed ~2.8 points over RNA-only (0.650→0.678), suggesting the image modality's value may be bottlenecked by encoder quality. Uncertainty: Whether upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to a much larger pretrained VIT-L can unlock additional multimodal signal, or whether the image contribution is fundamentally limited regardless of encoder. This experiment (config_037) tests exactly that: it takes the proven best configuration and swaps only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while keeping the validated scvi_n200 RNA encoder, multiprofile, avgpool, and weighted fusion. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it directly probes the single largest unexplored axis (image encoder capacity) on the current best configuration, with high information value: a gain confirms the image modality is underutilized and justifies further image-side tuning, while a flat result tells us to focus remaining budget on RNA-side or fusion refinements."
}

